	)
	(text "Li-Ion Charge Management Controller"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 192.532 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "19e2f47c-1a7f-42d2-8f93-2a0c2f267a9f")
	)
	(text "This sheet contains the relevant schematics responsible for powering the system,\nconsisting of a buck converter and a basic power mux system to switch between USB\nand battery power.\n\n- Jack Bradley"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 178.816 173.482 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2d2b9b34-7aef-4b6a-9869-b907d9d7271b")
	)
	(text "Power inputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.368 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "42c8bc9a-817d-4822-9cfe-237a784cb2ae")
	)
	(text "The ESP32 C3 Mini 1 is the predominant power consumer in this system, Table 6-5 in \nthe datasheet gives us an upper bound of ~340mA current draw with an input of 3.3 V\nat room temperature.\n\nWe'll assume a worst case of 20mA for the RGB LED, and another 5mA for the other\ncomponents in the system.\n\nAs a guesstimate, we expect roughly 340 + 20 + 5 = 365mA as our absolute worst\ncase current draw on our 3.3V line, and we will spec our components as such."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.224 184.404 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.1875)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "46bbd6a9-b010-4a72-bd69-4eb2658e1263")
	)
	(text "Power electronics"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.406 189.738 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "54cd96d8-fd42-4cb7-902e-fac155a5ee1b")
	)
	(text "TODO: Validate calcs on EN resistor divider"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.432 39.878 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6cc7070a-d8b6-4a9d-8f72-e9b8e809bcd9")
	)
	(text "The system operates in two main modes:\n 1. Battery powered (USB disconnected).\n 2. USB powered (powers system and charges battery).\n\nBattery is a 1S LiPo:\n 4.2V maximum safe voltage.\n 3.7V nominal voltage.\n 3.5V minimum healthy voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.716 26.924 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.1875)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "819fcedf-4580-484f-8a28-f16de7cb4fc6")
	)
	(text "Section 6.5 of the datasheet lists:\n - EN threshold high level sits between 1.14v - 1.22v\n - EN threshold low level sits between 0.91v - 1.09v\n\nFor the worst case where the system starts above the high threshold then dips down,\nit must reach 0.91v before it cuts off, in the worst case. We cutoff when the\nbattery reaches 3.5V.\n\nA 1.02M and 357k voltage divider achieves the desired 0.91v \n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.622 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
				(thickness 0.1875)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "98d2af9b-e42c-4eb4-85bf-d80a027d2585")
	)
	(text "USB / Battery VSYS power path\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.512 149.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b939ed23-ed86-48a2-a54f-0a78a15275d5")
	)
	(text "NOTE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 171.45 0)
